p(45,10,"I had hard work at it for several weeks; you see",
 "Jerry tells Grant how he stopped drinking. It was hard work, but his wife helped him, and now for ten years he has not tasted a drop.",
 "Jerry says that he had hard work at it for several weeks. He never did get drunk, but he found that he was not his own master, and that when the craving came on, it was hard to say no. He saw that one of them must give way, the drink devil or Jerry Barker. He said it should not be Jerry Barker, with God’s help. It was a struggle, and he wanted all the help he could get. Until he tried to break the habit, he did not know how strong it was. But Polly took great trouble to make sure that he had good food. When the craving came, he would get a cup of coffee or some peppermint, or read a little in his book, and that helped him. Sometimes he had to say over and over to himself, “Give up the drink or lose your soul! Give up the drink or break Polly’s heart!” But thanks be to God and his dear wife, his chains were broken, and now for ten years he has not tasted a drop and never wishes for it.",
 ["craving","knock under","habit","peppermint","chains","tasted"])
